Original poem — ‘Market Road’:
The road to market wakes before the sun,
its dust a bright and busy ghost of feet;
the baskets sway, the early songs are begun,
and every stone remembers where we meet.
By noon the heat has quietened every stall;
the road lies empty, patient, long and clear;
then evening brings us home, and one by one
we leave our footprints for the dawn to hear.
